<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raqqa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raqqa is a city on the north bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. Known in Hellenistic and Roman times as Nikephorion and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kallinikos">Kallinikos</a>, it was the residence of the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid</a> from 796 to 808, and in the 10th and 11th centuries it was held in turn by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamdanid-dynasty">Hamdanids</a> and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> such as the Numayrids. From 2014 to 2017 it was the de facto capital of the Islamic State group.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raqqa.jpg" alt="Raqqa" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User Zeledi on en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raqqa_2003-12-31.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1182 Kukbary of Harran defected and invited Saladin into the Jazira: its cities fell one by one, and on 12 June 1183 Zangi handed Aleppo to Saladin for Sinjar, Nusaybin and <b>Raqqa</b>, ending Zengid rule in Syria.</blockquote><a href="/empire/zengid-dynasty">Zengid dynasty · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>During the Iberian War, a Sasanian Persian army defeated the Byzantine army of Belisarius at Callinicum (<b>Raqqa</b>), in northern Syria, on Easter Saturday.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-19">19 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The army of Caliph Harun al-Rashid, far larger than any assembled before, left <b>Raqqa</b>, crossed Cilicia and the Taurus Mountains and invaded Byzantine Cappadocia.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-11">11 June in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Around 990, as Hamdanid power faded, their chief Waththab ibn Sabiq seized Harran, and the tribe went on to hold Saruj, <b>Raqqa</b> and for a time Edessa.</blockquote><a href="/state/numayrids">Numayrids</a></li></ul></section>
